From 35daede4c58559b8918f5d4e30674b538ac06081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:56:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] param-spec, rend-spec: Document HSDir one-request-per-circuit
 rules

Add the "hsdir_one_request_per_circ" and "hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop"
consensus parameters, note that HSV3MaxDescriptorSize also bounds the
request body a non-authority directory server will buffer, and state in
rend-spec that each descriptor fetch and upload is made on its own
circuit.

Companion to tor#41339.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 spec/param-spec.md              | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spec/param-spec.md b/spec/param-spec.md
index 6a86178f..105c7db8 100644
--- a/spec/param-spec.md
+++ b/spec/param-spec.md
@@ -347,6 +347,11 @@ will upload its descriptor to.
 Min: 1. Max: 128. Default: 4
 
 "HSV3MaxDescriptorSize" -- Maximum descriptor size (in bytes).
+On relays that are not directory authorities, this also bounds the body of
+an HTTP request that the directory server will buffer: a request whose
+declared or actual body is at least this many bytes (or at least 16 MB, if
+that is smaller) is rejected without being fully buffered. Directory authorities
+keep the 16 MB limit.
 Min: 1. Max: INT32_MAX. Default: 50000
 
 "hs_service_max_rdv_failures" -- This parameter determines the
@@ -492,6 +497,28 @@ First appeared: 0.4.9.0-alpha-dev.
     First appeared: 0.4.9.0-alpha-dev.
 ```
 
+"hsdir_one_request_per_circ" -- If 1, an onion service directory closes,
+with reason RESOURCELIMIT, any circuit on which it receives a second onion
+service descriptor fetch or upload. If 0, it only counts such circuits.
+Whatever the value, each such circuit is counted once (in the DoS
+heartbeat, and as `tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_circ_reused"}` on the
+MetricsPort). The relay torrc option `HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit` (0, 1, or
+auto) overrides this parameter.
+Min: 0. Max: 1. Default: 0.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
+"hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop" -- If 1, an onion service directory
+refuses, with an HTTP 503 response, an onion service descriptor fetch or
+upload whose previous hop is not a relay that it recognizes (one in its
+consensus, or for which it has a descriptor). If 0, it only counts such
+requests. Whatever the value, they are counted (in the DoS heartbeat, and
+as `tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_unknown_prev_hop"}` on the MetricsPort).
+The relay torrc option `HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop` (0, 1, or auto)
+overrides this parameter. This parameter is independent of
+"refuseunknownexits": changing either one does not affect the other.
+Min: 0. Max: 1. Default: 0.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
 <a id="param-spec.txt-10"></a>
 
 ## Padding-related parameters {#padding}
diff --git a/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md b/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
index 066f34d4..e3d6faa8 100644
--- a/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
+++ b/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
@@ -433,6 +433,14 @@ version which is "3" in this case.
 
 These requests must be made anonymously, on circuits not used for
 anything else.
+Each descriptor fetch and each descriptor upload MUST be made on its own
+circuit: a client or service MUST NOT send a second such request on a
+circuit that already carried one.
+An onion service directory MAY close a circuit that carries more than one
+such request (see "hsdir_one_request_per_circ" in the
+[parameter specification](../param-spec.md)), and MAY refuse a request whose
+previous hop it does not recognize as a relay (see
+"hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop").
 
 The legacy [".z" suffix][dot-z] is **not** supported for these URLs.
 
